# ================ PART 3 (CM213-Low-1): the l36 supplement's counts are pinned to the commit ================
# The supplement prints "all matching files : 25" and "prose files that quote it : 3", listing gen_manifest.md among
# the prose. Neither reproduces at its own commit. Measured on a detached archive of df1d8c5 below: 24 matching
# files, 2 of them the landing's own artefacts, 20 retained logs and 2 prose files, and the prose files are
# gen_critic_tb_l34.md and gen_tdd_step2b.md, NOT gen_manifest.md.
# WHY: I generated the supplement in my WORKING TREE, where the next landing's manifest row was already present and
# quoted the literal figure; the row as committed paraphrases it instead. So those two numbers were artefacts of an
# uncommitted tree state rather than facts about a commit.
# WHAT STANDS: the citation itself, 20 retained logs, which reproduces exactly, and which the supplement had already
# made self-stable by excluding the landing's own artefacts by name.
# THE RULE THIS EARNS: a count taken in a dirty tree is not a fact about a commit. Any figure a record states about
# the repository is measured on a detached archive of the commit it names, not on the working tree.

